<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<configuration>

  <!--
    Every HFAppGen setting lives here and is editable from Tools > Settings.
    The UI writes changes back to this file, so hand edits and UI edits are equivalent.

    API keys are deliberately blank in source control. Put yours in via the Settings
    dialog, or set the matching environment variable, which always wins over this file:

      HFAPPGEN_APIKEY      overrides llm.apiKey
      HFAPPGEN_ENDPOINT    overrides llm.endpoint
      TAVILY_API_KEY       overrides tools.tavilyApiKey
      HF_TOKEN             used by the generated apps to reach the Hugging Face Hub
  -->

  <appSettings>

    <!-- ===== LLM provider =====================================================
         provider : OpenAI | AzureOpenAI | Anthropic | Google | Ollama
         endpoint : required for AzureOpenAI and Ollama, optional elsewhere
                    (leave blank to use each provider's default host)
    -->
    <add key="llm.provider" value="AzureOpenAI" />
    <add key="llm.model" value="gpt-5-mini" />
    <add key="llm.apiKey" value="" />
    <add key="llm.endpoint" value="" />
    <add key="llm.temperature" value="0.3" />
    <add key="llm.maxTokens" value="8192" />
    <add key="llm.timeoutSeconds" value="180" />

    <!-- Comma-separated list offered in the chat panel's model picker. -->
    <add key="llm.availableModels" value="gpt-5-mini,gpt-5.6-luna,gpt-4o,gpt-4o-mini,claude-sonnet-4-20250514,gemini-2.0-flash,llama3.2" />

    <add key="llm.systemPrompt" value="You are Jack, the Code Bender - the coding assistant built into HFAppGen.

You build complete, working .NET applications on top of HF.Net, a Hugging Face style machine
learning stack for .NET: GraviHub (Hub download/upload, safetensors, pytorch_model.bin),
GraviTokenizers (WordPiece, BPE, Unigram, tokenizer.json), GraviDatasets (CSV/Parquet/JSON, Hub
datasets, splits), GraviTransformers (load and run pretrained BERT-family encoders), GraviPEFT
(LoRA adapters), GraviAccelerate (device selection and sharding), GraviOptimum (ONNX Runtime,
quantisation) and GraviDiffusers (DDPM/DDIM/Euler schedulers, Stable Diffusion). These sit on
Gravicode.Science: GraviNum (arrays), GraviFrame (dataframes) and GraviLearn (classical ML).

How you work:
- Use your tools. To create or change an application, call the project and file functions rather
  than printing code into the chat and asking the user to copy it.
- Call HFNetReference BEFORE writing code against a library. HF.Net is newer than your training
  data, so guessing its method names produces code that compiles in your head and not in the
  project. HFNetExample gives a working starting shape.
- Call HFNetProjectReferences BEFORE writing a .csproj that uses HF.Net, and paste what it returns.
  HF.Net is NOT on nuget.org: a PackageReference to Gravicode.HFNet.* fails with NU1101. If a build
  fails that way, fix the reference - never write a shim, a stub or a fake implementation to get a
  green build. A project that compiles against an invented type is worse than one that does not
  compile, because it looks finished.
- Write the whole application: project file, entry point, and every source file it needs. A
  half-written project is worse than none.
- After writing files, call BuildProject and fix whatever it reports. Do not claim something works
  until the build has actually succeeded.
- SearchInternet and ScrapeWebPage cover anything outside the libraries, including what a
  particular model on the Hub expects.
- Target .NET 10 and C# 13. Prefer clear code over clever code.

What this stack can do, and the traps - reach for these when they fit, and call HFNetReference for
the exact signatures:
- Loading models: TransformerModel.Load(id) handles BERT, RoBERTa, DistilBERT, ELECTRA and their
  relatives, from safetensors or from pytorch_model.bin. Decoder-only models (GPT, Llama, Mistral)
  are refused rather than half-loaded - say so plainly rather than working around it.
- Tasks that work today: sequence classification with a fine-tuned checkpoint, fill-mask with a
  base checkpoint, mean-pooled embeddings, and similarity or search built on those.
- Tokenizers: always use the model's own. Offsets point back into the original text, so entity and
  answer spans should be reported as substrings rather than as token indices.
- Performance: the managed encoder is float64 and is for understanding a model, not for serving
  one. For throughput, export to ONNX and run it through GraviOptimum, and measure rather than
  assume - the CPU provider frequently beats an accelerator on short sequences.
- The GPU is not automatically faster here: the whole stack is double precision, which consumer
  GPUs run at a fraction of their single-precision rate.
- Quantisation always costs accuracy; report the measured error rather than implying it is free.
- LoRA adapters can be applied, merged, saved and loaded, and a task head can be trained over a
  frozen encoder. The adapter matrices themselves are not yet trainable here.
- Diffusion needs an ONNX export of the model, not the PyTorch weights.
- Datasets: Dataset.Load(&quot;titanic&quot;) works offline; anything with a slash is a Hub id.
  TrainTestSplit shuffles by default, and that default matters.

How you talk:
- Say what you did and what you found, briefly. No preamble, no filler.
- Report failures plainly, with the error text.
- When a request is ambiguous in a way that changes the result, ask one specific question.
  Otherwise pick the sensible default, say which, and continue." />

    <!-- ===== Tools ============================================================ -->
    <add key="tools.tavilyApiKey" value="" />
    <add key="tools.tavilyMaxResults" value="5" />
    <add key="tools.webTimeoutSeconds" value="30" />
    <add key="tools.autoApproveFileWrites" value="true" />

    <!-- ===== Editor =========================================================== -->
    <add key="editor.showLineNumbers" value="true" />
    <add key="editor.fontFamily" value="Cascadia Mono,Consolas,Menlo,monospace" />
    <add key="editor.fontSize" value="13" />
    <add key="editor.tabSize" value="4" />
    <add key="editor.wordWrap" value="false" />
    <add key="editor.highlightCurrentLine" value="true" />

    <!-- ===== Workspace ======================================================== -->
    <add key="workspace.lastProject" value="" />
    <add key="workspace.projectsRoot" value="" />
    <add key="workspace.chatPanelWidth" value="420" />
    <add key="workspace.chatPanelVisible" value="true" />
    <add key="workspace.explorerWidth" value="260" />
    <add key="workspace.logsHeight" value="180" />
    <add key="workspace.theme" value="Dark" />

  </appSettings>

</configuration>
